  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "I wanted lighter, more playful entertainment; military science fiction and a space-franchise finale did not fit that mood.",
    "The Mummy shared a supernatural theme with Hocus Pocus, but I was looking for its playful tone rather than supernatural action.",
    "I could not establish any personal relevance for the untitled items, so I would skip them rather than assume they suited me."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seemed to treat an interest in supernatural stories as an interest in action and spectacle more broadly.",
    "Recognizable movie titles alone were not enough to make these feel connected to what I wanted next."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The lighter mood I associate with Hocus Pocus and Blockers mattered more to me than a shared fantasy element.",
    "I rarely interact without a clear reason to expect a match, and the unidentified items gave me no basis for that expectation."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices loosely connected to my movie interests but missed my current preference for playful, lighter entertainment."
}"}
